  "text_pages": [
    "Exchange/Visiting Pre-Arrival Guide - b. International Student Organization (ISO)\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nInternational Student Organization (ISO)\nAbout the ISO\nGreetings from ISO, The International Student Organization at Hankuk University of Foreign Studies.\nThe ISO was first established in 2003 for the purpose of providing information necessary for college life and opportunities for\nexchange and visiting students\nat HUFS to experience Korean culture. We offer a variety of events each semester and are dedicated to promoting globalization and intercultural exchange among HUFS students. We hope you enjoy your life in Korea with us and experience the true meaning of our university motto,\nCome to HUFS, Meet the World!\nYou can find more info on their Instagram @hufsisoseoul / @hufsisoglobal\nISO: seoul Campus chapter\nPR Team\nPromotes ISO with ad posters, social media communication, and souvenirs\nATTI Team\nOrganizes events that promote Korean cultural experiences and intercultural exchange\nBUDDY Team\nManages the BUDDY program, a friend-matching program between Korean and international students\nGAT Team\nOrganizes Give and Take (GAT), a 1:1 Language Exchange Program\nPlease refer to the ISO Schedule for details about events hosted by each team.\nInquiries regarding school life, facilities, academic affairs, etc., and visits from anyone who wants to have fun with us ISO members are welcome!\nISO Office (\n아방\nor “Abang”) Information\nLocation:\nMinerva Complex, #B01\nOffice Hours:\nWeekdays 09:00-17:00, except during exam periods\nAny inquiry regarding school life, facilities, academic affairs, etc. is welcomed.\nContact Information\nFacebook:\nhttps://www.facebook.com/HUFSISOSEOUL\nInstagram:\n@hufsisoseoul\nKakaotalk:\nhufsiso\nGmail:\nhufsiso@gmail.com\nISO: Global Campus chapter\nPR Team\nPromotes ISO with ad posters, social media communication, and souvenirs\nExchange Team\nManages the BUDDY program, a friend-matching program between Korean and international students\nPlanning & Culture Team\nOrganizes every event including BRIDGE BUS PROGRAM for international students\nInquiries regarding school life, facilities, academic affairs, etc., and visits from anyone who wants to have fun with us ISO members are welcome!\nISO Office (\n아방\nor “Abang”) Information\nLocation:\nStudent Hall #105-1\nOffice Hours:\nWeekdays\n10:00 - 16:00\nAny inquiry regarding school life, facilities, academic affairs, etc. is welcomed.\nContact Information\nFac\nebook:\nhttps://www.facebook.com/HUFSISOGLOBAL\nInstagram:\n@hufsisoglobal\nGmail:\niso.hufsglobal@gmail.com\nYoutube:\n한국외대 ISO Global Campus\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nReport abuse"
  ],
